Subject: [PATCH] Put srtp.h where <srtp2/srtp.h> looks for it, in the tree

libdatachannel -- the WebRTC library the calls are built on -- includes
<srtp2/srtp.h>, which is the layout libsrtp's own install rules write. Built
against libsrtp's source tree, as cmake-everywhere's port does, the header is
there as include/srtp.h and <srtp2/srtp.h> finds nothing.

A copy is put beside it, so both layouts answer: the store entry that keeps
this tree then carries srtp2/srtp.h, which is what the port's CHECK_HEADER
asks of it.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -301,6 +301,14 @@
 install(TARGETS srtp2 DESTINATION lib
   EXPORT libSRTPTargets
 )
 
+# mux: libdatachannel includes <srtp2/srtp.h>, the layout the install rules
+# below write; in the source tree the header is include/srtp.h, and a build
+# against the tree as it is finds nothing. A copy is put where it is looked
+# for, so both layouts answer.
+file(MAKE_DIRECTORY ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/include/srtp2)
+file(COPY ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/include/srtp.h
+  DESTINATION ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/include/srtp2)
+
 install(FILES include/srtp.h crypto/include/auth.h
   crypto/include/cipher.h
   crypto/include/crypto_types.h
